# Database Access & ORM

## Choice

- **Prisma:** Strong typing, migrations, good DX; recommended for most projects
- **Drizzle:** SQL-like, lightweight, performant
- **TypeORM:** Decorators, common in NestJS

## Prisma

- **Schema:** Define models, relations, indexes; `prisma generate`; migrations with `prisma migrate`
- **Client:** Singleton (e.g. global in dev to avoid many instances); connect at startup
- **Queries:** Use include/select to avoid N+1; paginate with take/skip or cursor
- **Transactions:** `prisma.$transaction([...])` for multiple writes; interactive `$transaction(async (tx) => ...)` when needed
- **Errors:** Handle unique constraint, not found; map to domain or HTTP errors

## Migrations

- Version migrations; never edit applied migrations; test on copy of prod data
- Prisma: `migrate deploy` in CI; Drizzle: run migration script

## Conventions

- One client per app; use transactions for multi-step writes; validate input before write; use parameterized queries (ORM does this)

## Anti-Patterns

- N+1 queries; raw SQL with concatenated input; no migrations; multiple client instances

